      },
      {
        "id": "team-chris-walters",
        "slug": "chris-walters",
        "status": "published",
        "data": {
          "name": "Chris Walters",
          "role": "Realtor®",
          "credentials": "Buyer Specialist",
          "tagline": "Would Rather Be Riding—But He’ll Help You Move First",
          "bio": [
            {
              "_type": "block",
              "_key": "b9064eac0270",
              "style": "normal",
              "markDefs": [],
              "children": [
                {
                  "_type": "span",
                  "_key": "cd23889604be",
                  "text": "Chris came to real estate after careers in microelectronics and as a master electrician—because apparently, one career path was too boring. He started his own microelectronics business, worked for a big corporation, then became an electrician because why not? He was qualified. Now he helps people buy and sell homes while secretly cataloging every electrical code violation he sees. (Don’t worry, he’s polite about it.)",
                  "marks": []
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "_type": "block",
              "_key": "411cd6cafbfd",
              "style": "normal",
              "markDefs": [],
              "children": [
                {
                  "_type": "span",
                  "_key": "73f951a05028",
                  "text": "When he’s not helping empty nesters navigate downsizing logistics, he’s either on his motorcycle or thinking about being on his motorcycle. Occasionally both at the same time, which Randyl has asked him to stop doing.",
                  "marks": []
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "_type": "block",
              "_key": "114648271e50",
              "style": "normal",
              "markDefs": [],
              "children": [
                {
                  "_type": "span",
                  "_key": "90f940a6a27e",
                  "text": "His clients describe him as “unsettlingly helpful” and “the only realtor who actually understood what the home inspector was talking about.” One couple tried to hire him to just follow them around and fix things. He politely declined. Probably.",
                  "marks": []
                }
              ]
            }
          ],
          "email": "chriswalters@KW.com",
          "sort_order": 3
        }
